From c565ac7f52d6b1970fb7cf3b101efedb873a6253 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 00:08:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(app): judge a boring bar's head and shank on its
 cutting feeds
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The rapid law (#103) judged the bar's whole body on its rapids and the
envelope verdict judged the nose's cut, so the head and shank rode
every plunge, lead and pass unjudged against the stock. The new
turning_feeds law samples each feed of a Bore tool along its length.
At each instant it reads the bar's head (flute_len up the axis) and
shank (shank_len above it), at the spans turning::bar_spans gives,
against the revolved part, and against the stock less the drills
ahead, the turning ops ahead, the program ahead's faced end, this
path's earlier feeds and this feed's own kerf up to that instant. The
nose's own cut is never judged here. A body in the part or in stock
still standing is a ShankHit on that move, which blocks the post (one
per move; a move the solid law already named is not named twice).

The Meridian context in generate is built once and shared by the rapid
and feed laws; turning_rapids' meridian helpers become pub(super).

Pins (turning_bore):
- a_bar_whose_head_rides_the_uncut_band_above_its_nose_is_convicted
  (Ø10 bar, Ø12 bore over a Ø10.6 pilot: the head's edge rides the
  uncut band above the nose; fails on main, which posts it clean)
- a_stepped_bar_whose_shank_rubs_the_wall_during_the_ride_is_convicted
  (head Ø8, shank Ø12, Ø14 bore: ShankHit on the part on the ride)
- a_bored_op_runs_clean_in_the_document stays clean.

Fixes #146

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
